WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:07.870
Speaker 1: Let's talk next about a new poll
from CBS News that really highlights the degree

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.830
to which we're in serious trouble in this
country because of the things that people

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:17.770
believe disproportionately right wingers,
disproportionately, Republicans disproportionately.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:23.840
Trump is now some will write in and say, you
know, David, you are overexaggerating the

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.550
degree to which these problems are among the
American right.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.300
And I would say, no, I'm not.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:32.250
The data actually tells us that that's exactly
the case.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:38.820
So let's take a look at at the poll, CBS News.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.030
Still more to learn about January 6th.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:44.220
Most Americans say some of the data here is
concerning and some is not.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:49.980
We'll look at some of the questions when it
comes to the January 6th attack on the capital.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.230
Seventy two percent of Americans say there
is more to learn, and twenty eight percent

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.280
say we know all there is to know.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.450
This is one of those questions where in principle
there's nothing concerning here.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:07.719
It was a complex event in the sense that it
involved a lot of moving parts.

00:01:07.719 --> 00:01:12.859
It was multifaceted in that it was Donald
Trump and Republicans and right wing media

00:01:12.859 --> 00:01:15.759
and others fomenting the idea that the election
was stolen.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:19.649
And I would agree there is still more to learn.

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:23.289
The problem is a lot of the people who say
there's still more to learn, what they mean

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:28.319
by that is even at the top level, that this
was violent.

00:01:28.319 --> 00:01:32.740
Right wingers inspired by Republicans with
the lie that the election was stolen, which

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.840
it wasn't, that's not even something that
they would accept.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:43.609
So this is actually quite concerning among
Republicans when they were asked about the

00:01:43.609 --> 00:01:47.189
actions of those who forced their way into
the Capitol.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:53.569
The number of Republicans that strongly disapprove
of the riots has declined by 12 points.

00:01:53.569 --> 00:02:00.919
In other words, more people now, at least
to some degree, approve of what took place

00:02:00.919 --> 00:02:02.039
on January 6th.

00:02:02.039 --> 00:02:05.069
And most of that is in somewhat approve.

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:09.069
There's an increase in people that disapprove,
but only somewhat.

00:02:09.069 --> 00:02:15.260
And so the point here is the strong Republican
opposition condemnation of what happened on

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:19.930
January 6th has declined 12 points since January.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:25.530
What how would you describe what happened
at the Capitol?

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:32.819
Fifty five percent of Trump voters describe
what happened at the Capitol as a defense

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:42.900
of freedom, and fifty one percent of Trump
describe what happened at the Capitol as patriotism.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.980
This is absolutely unconscionable.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:51.430
Now, if you're looking at the graphic, 20
percent of Trump voters call what happened

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.430
on the 6th an insurrection.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:58.890
I'm actually surprised that even 20 percent
of them are willing to call it that.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:02.650
This is the type of now, I'm not saying these
people are Nazis.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.329
That's not what I'm saying.

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:10.019
What I am saying, though, is that this level
of cognitive dissonance with what took place

00:03:10.019 --> 00:03:16.950
on that day is the type of thing that created
a vacuum in which Hitler was able to seize

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.959
power in nineteen thirties Germany.

00:03:18.959 --> 00:03:20.739
I'm not saying anyone is Hitler.

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:22.860
I'm not saying anyone is a Nazi.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:27.129
But this is the type of thing where when you
see people this disconnected, 55 percent of

00:03:27.129 --> 00:03:33.239
voters say those riots, that violent insurrection
coup attempt, that was a defense of freedom.

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:35.439
That's really, really dangerous stuff.

00:03:35.439 --> 00:03:41.590
And in particular, it was a riot fomented
by the then sitting president.

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:45.780
Sixty six percent of all respondents say that
US democracy today is threatened and thirty

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.239
four percent say to secure.

00:03:48.239 --> 00:03:52.049
This is a really complicated question.

00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:55.230
And unfortunately, it's like I don't even
know that these polls give us what we need

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:00.959
to know, because there are people on the left
who believe democracy is threatened because

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:05.269
Trump and Republicans tried to overturn the
overturn the results of the election.

00:04:05.269 --> 00:04:10.329
There are people on the right who think that
democracy is threatened because they believe

00:04:10.329 --> 00:04:13.909
that Joe Biden didn't really win and is somehow
now the president.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:18.120
So even a simple question like democracy is
threatened today.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:24.700
The answer doesn't really tell us much because
the reasons why people say yes very dramatically.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:29.610
The bottom line is this was an attempt to
overturn the election results based on the

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:36.500
lie that it was stolen, that riotous insurrection
was fomented by the then sitting president.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:42.380
It was it was bad enough how the right reacted
at the time.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:47.990
But six months later, they are sort of you
could call it a revisionist history.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:52.920
You could call it a group delusion, whatever
you call it.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:57.790
The percentage of Republicans who don't think
it was that serious has gone up in the five

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:00.350
months since of six months since it took place.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:04.940
And the percentage of Republicans and Trump
voters who say it was a positive act to defend

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:06.690
freedom has gone up dramatically.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.440
So what is the takeaway?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.850
The takeaway continues to be, number one.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.690
I don't know how we fix this.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.190
I just have I'm out of ideas, guys.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:20.420
Number two, the extremist faction of the Republican
Party is the dominant wing.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:27.820
If you are a viable Republican in most ways
like Liz Cheney is.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:30.830
But you think, guys, this election stuff makes
us look stupid.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.020
You are now apparently in the minority in
the Republican Party, at least as far as they're

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.220
willing to admit publicly.

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:42.830
And then final takeaway, Joe Manchin and Kirsten
Sinema, two Democratic senators who insist

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:48.220
that we want to find common ground with Republicans,
we want to work together.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:54.960
We need to find compromise that is between
what Democrats and Republicans want.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.750
These are the people that you are trying to
do that with the people.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:03.740
Fifty five percent who say the riots were
a defense of freedom, only 20 percent of whom

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:06.490
are willing to say it was an attempted insurrection.

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:10.110
Joe Manchin and Kirsten Sinema, how exactly
do you find common ground with those people?

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.380
It's a genuine question.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.680
We're really, really in trouble.

